#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244022 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124590 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f306cf2-6881-5948-90bd-4e0ce98b4116" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Matrix Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af81d6e6-3cad-5c8a-99a9-13bc107158af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447854} {:answer/id #uuid "4921fc50-ffd5-5037-85e5-4437f4da71a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447855}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4921fc50-ffd5-5037-85e5-4437f4da71a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447855} :answer-field/id #uuid "31478e71-bb60-536e-8adc-4001942eec0d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448967} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7871ce40-048e-5347-b7c4-782324459d1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447856} {:answer/id #uuid "54e54e39-08f5-53d6-b847-857578e17e69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447857}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54e54e39-08f5-53d6-b847-857578e17e69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447857} :answer-field/id #uuid "19481cce-f1a9-5f87-8a34-93aac01ae946" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448968} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5f3b98c-c4eb-5c6c-ace2-f7e5a2fd7de5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447858} {:answer/id #uuid "3b35c2e7-4cc8-5a23-9d0a-9ee7e8200d90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447859}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b35c2e7-4cc8-5a23-9d0a-9ee7e8200d90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447859} :answer-field/id #uuid "e99ca2b0-1668-5738-9b06-76be8f1daed7" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448969} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0081fe2-ba7a-565b-921c-11dc8bd79c3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447860} {:answer/id #uuid "fc911407-1e5d-58b7-8982-c859119fe356" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447861}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0081fe2-ba7a-565b-921c-11dc8bd79c3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447860} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7b988c1-5329-5cf2-9e2b-7bef7867ab8c" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448970}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "89286e95-724b-57e9-aee8-7d71e484cafb" :question/math-academy-id "q-107113" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R$ and its subset $A={[\\begin{aligned}0 & a \\\\ b & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,a,b\\in R}.$  \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ is closed under matrix addition\n- **II.** $A$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- **III.** $A$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n- **IV.** $A$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If ${A}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & {a}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{1} & 0\\end{aligned}]$ and ${A}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & {a}_{2} \\\\ {b}_{2} & 0\\end{aligned}]$ are two matrices from $A,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & {a}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{1} & 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 & {a}_{2} \\\\ {b}_{2} & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & {a}_{1}+{a}_{2} \\\\ {b}_{1}+{b}_{2} & 0\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich is a matrix from $A.$ So, $A$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & a \\\\ b & 0\\end{aligned}]$ is an element of $A$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kA & =k[\\begin{aligned}0 & a \\\\ b & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & ka \\\\ kb & 0\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a matrix from $A.$ So, $A$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement IV is false. $A$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378348 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124590 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f306cf2-6881-5948-90bd-4e0ce98b4116" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Matrix Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "913e0931-a878-5504-b8b6-00f819edf9a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453210} {:answer/id #uuid "461ff5c7-f262-59e0-9e6a-5ccd795fb660" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453211}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "913e0931-a878-5504-b8b6-00f819edf9a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453210} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e294ac2-b715-5c6e-b139-8e2b8b489e3a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454355} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e10c2846-bfa3-5599-a565-ba95e776088c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453212} {:answer/id #uuid "dfd1227a-6d81-5364-a894-22a85a885507" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453213}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dfd1227a-6d81-5364-a894-22a85a885507" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453213} :answer-field/id #uuid "5eca9126-955c-5afe-833c-fc32a0b53bb9" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454356} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "076b77e2-6bf3-5918-86f9-98829053c98d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453214} {:answer/id #uuid "d46b15b3-6f74-5c05-b218-76f6180d184c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453215}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "076b77e2-6bf3-5918-86f9-98829053c98d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453214} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab876604-ae7b-5692-8d5d-ac2e83bc51d1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454357} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a38d2c4-5da1-58d9-ad2f-9024e96c37be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453216} {:answer/id #uuid "9261a407-a47e-58cf-876d-d1ebb17244ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453217}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9261a407-a47e-58cf-876d-d1ebb17244ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453217} :answer-field/id #uuid "5823a91a-8b7b-550d-a8ed-1b40a6c306e7" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454358}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "29e169b1-20c5-5789-9178-14e4b85ea9c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-107117" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R,$ and its subset $S$ containing $2\\times 2$ matrices that are not invertible. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $S$ is closed under matrix addition\n- **II.** $S$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- **III.** $S$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n- **IV.** $S$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is false. For example, if ${A}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ and ${A}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],$ then\n${A}_{1}$ and ${A}_{2}$ each contain a row consisting only of zeros, so they are not invertible. However,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis invertible. So, $S$ is *not* closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, if $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix that is not invertible then $det(A)=0$ and therefore for all $\\alpha \\in R$ \n\n$$\ndet(\\alpha A)={\\alpha }^{2}\\cdot det(A)={\\alpha }^{2}\\cdot 0=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore,  $S$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $S$ is a *not* subspace because it's not closed under addition.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496300 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124591 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b1bb974-826a-590f-8d32-cdc868ca827c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Polynomial Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2121065c-b843-5046-8de5-d3cd11c91cc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495580} {:answer/id #uuid "40147242-1ff3-5589-bd5f-2562944166ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495657} {:answer/id #uuid "7c969901-88f0-5143-89a5-a836078136cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495777} {:answer/id #uuid "8ee5cbac-98dc-5804-b9ee-b5c755e31be5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495825} {:answer/id #uuid "ca0b96fa-4065-5336-8b0e-48692fa39925" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495950}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7c969901-88f0-5143-89a5-a836078136cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495777} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf373aed-aad4-52b7-aa07-ba88e991e0e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496182}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b24b6cb2-194b-5c78-a36d-8250b69a2b91" :question/math-academy-id "q-94614" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${R}_{2}[t]$ of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $2,$ and its subset $A$ containing all polynomials of the form $a{t}^{2},$ where $a\\in R.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ is closed under polynomial addition\n\nII. $A$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n\nIII. $A$ is a subspace of ${R}_{2}[t]$\n\nIV. $A$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}_{2}[t]$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If $f(t)={a}_{1}{t}^{2}$ and $g(t)={a}_{2}{t}^{2}$ are two polynomials from $A,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)+g(t) & ={a}_{1}{t}^{2}+{a}_{2}{t}^{2} \\\\  & =({a}_{1}+{a}_{2}){t}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a polynomial from $A.$ So, $A$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $f(t)=a{t}^{2}\\in A$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kf(t) & =k(a{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =(ka){t}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a polynomial from $A.$ So, $A$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true while statement IV is false. $A$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\""}]}
